I  I really enjoy to a war war hammer these  are two franchises that I've wanted to  to meet for years and they both have  unique aspects that kind of that they  were there were meant to be together  you've got the grand battles of fantasy  of Warhammer and also the large  campaigns giant maps and massive amounts  of infantry from total war and they both  work together wonderfully in a way that  I've been hoping for since I've been  about 14 total war war hammer was pretty  cool I struggled with some areas there  was less of a tutorial than in earlier  total war game so there was quite a bit  of assumed knowledge at least in the  state that is currently in right now I  know they're still working on some  things which is contributed to the delay  things like balancing but I found early  on it was easy to forget that you had a  settlement way back where that needed to  be defended each race plays very  differently the humans are kind of like  your most classical total war factions  with the addition of magic and Griffin's  whereas dwarves are very defensive and  focus on artillery and even have a book  of grudges where they take note of any  time you've stepped against them and  then there's things like green skins who  have to constantly fight about their  entire campaign or they just evolved  into bickering and killing themselves I  think the fantasy definitely added to  the experience not that I didn't like  the total war settings where it was just  like a bunch of dudes who were different  forms of military but this just felt  very like a movie esque it felt really  cool if I like you're in the middle of a  big fantasy warfare setting and I don't  think I can think of any other games  that really give you that large-scale  real-time combat feel with fantasy  creatures what are most interesting  additions to tell a war warhammer our  story based battles and he requests so  sometimes battles will pop up in the  campaign map that have kind of a  scenario attached to 