 a  green-skinned army and dress all my orks  in pink vests and send them all into  battle but unfortunately at the moment  we can't quite make the pink orcs this  does feel really similar to other total  war games I think what makes it  different is if you really pay attention  to the battle and you just look at your  creatures and you're like a massive  swarms of bats as I said or your heroes  are actually huge werewolves and things  like that that is so different it's like  a completely familiar total war format  with this other injection of a really  cool fantasy theme the other thing works  quite well from what I've seen so far I  think the Warhammer franchise in the  Warhammer law adds a lot to total war  previously took war felt like you were  kind of creating your own game and your  own story now with the addition of years  of law from the Warhammer franchise  we're getting to know characters we get  to know a world beyond what we can just  see on a map it's not just a historical  version of our wide world so that  already adds a lot to the world a total  war and then like I said you have things  like goblins orcs dragons vampire bats  as well as a slew of magic so really  total war has been begging to the  fantasy element to be injected into it  for years and I have to say it's pretty  exciting and what they have made with  these two giant franchises finally  meeting is pretty great so far  you

